/-
# The Boltzmann Bridge X — The Lattice of Filtrations and Order-Functoriality

This file extends **Boltzmann Bridge IX** (`Applications.BoltzmannBridge.InterleavingFunctor`)
along its own Future Directions 2 and 5, fusing three previously separate layers
of the persistence catalog into a single order-theoretic picture:

* the **representation theorem** of Bridge IX (`weightEquiv`, `ofWeight`,
  `weight_surjective`), which identifies `Filtration α` with the monotone,
  `∅`-grounded functions `Finset α → ℝ`;
* the **isometry formula** of Bridge VIII
  (`eInterleavingDist_eq_weightSupEDist`), which pins the interleaving emetric to
  the sup-distance of weights;
* the **contravariant pullback functor** of Bridge IX (`pullback`,
  `pullback_id`, `pullback_comp`).

## The synthesis

Bridge IX showed the carrier `Filtration α` *is* (up to `weightEquiv`) a set of
functions closed under pointwise `max`/`min` — because both defining constraints
`w ∅ ≤ 0` and `Monotone w` are preserved by `⊔` and `⊓`.  Hence:

* **The pointwise order** `F ≤ G ↔ ∀ σ, F.weight σ ≤ G.weight σ` makes
  `Filtration α` a `PartialOrder` (antisymmetry is Bridge VII's `ext_weight`).
* **`Filtration α` is a `Lattice`**: `(F ⊔ G).weight = F.weight ⊔ G.weight`,
  `(F ⊓ G).weight = F.weight ⊓ G.weight` (`weight_sup`, `weight_inf`).
* **The pullback functor is a lattice homomorphism**: it is `Monotone`
  (`pullback_mono`) and commutes with `⊔` and `⊓` (`pullback_sup`,
  `pullback_inf`) — because precomposition with `·.image f` is pointwise.
* **`weightEquiv` is an order isomorphism** (`weightOrderIso`): the representation
  of Bridge IX is not merely a bijection but an iso of partial orders.

## The metric–order bridge (cross-domain)

Combining the lattice order with Bridge VIII's isometry collapses the absolute
value: **between comparable filtrations the interleaving distance is the
sup-*gap*** (`eInterleavingDist_of_le`):

> `F ≤ G  ⟹  eInterleavingDist F G = ⨆ σ, ENNReal.ofReal (G.weight σ - F.weight σ)`.

In particular the join and meet are nonexpansive contractions of a pair
(`eInterleavingDist_sup_le`, `eInterleavingDist_inf_le`).

## Direction 5 — faithfulness

Bridge IX proved `pullback` along a *surjection* is an isometry.  Here we add the
companion faithfulness statement: `pullback` along a surjection is **injective**
(`pullback_injective_of_surjective`) — distinct filtrations stay distinct, so the
persistence functor is faithful on the subcategory of surjections.

## Main results

* `instPartialOrderFiltration`, `weight_le_iff` — the pointwise order.
* `instLatticeFiltration`, `weight_sup`, `weight_inf` — the lattice structure.
* `pullback_mono`, `pullback_sup`, `pullback_inf` — pullback is a lattice hom.
* `weightOrderIso` — the representation is an order isomorphism.
* `eInterleavingDist_of_le` — the metric–order bridge.
* `eInterleavingDist_sup_le`, `eInterleavingDist_inf_le` — join/meet are short.
* `pullback_injective_of_surjective` — faithfulness (Direction 5).
-/
import Mathlib
import Applications.BoltzmannBridge.HigherPersistence
import Applications.BoltzmannBridge.PersistenceStability
import Applications.BoltzmannBridge.BottleneckStability
import Applications.BoltzmannBridge.InterleavingMetric
import Applications.BoltzmannBridge.InterleavingClosure
import Applications.BoltzmannBridge.InterleavingIsometry
import Applications.BoltzmannBridge.InterleavingFunctor

open Finset BigOperators
open scoped ENNReal

namespace BoltzmannBridge

namespace Filtration

variable {α β γ : Type*}

/-! ## The pointwise order on filtrations -/

-- !-- `le F G := ∀ σ, F.weight σ ≤ G.weight σ`; refl/trans are pointwise, and
-- !-- antisymmetry is `ext_weight (funext (le_antisymm …))` (Bridge VII). -- !--
/-- **The pointwise order on filtrations.**  `F ≤ G` means `F.weight σ ≤ G.weight σ`
for every simplex `σ`.  Antisymmetry is Bridge VII's `ext_weight`: a filtration is
its weight function. -/
instance instPartialOrderFiltration : PartialOrder (Filtration α) where
  le F G := ∀ σ, F.weight σ ≤ G.weight σ
  le_refl F σ := le_refl _
  le_trans F G H h₁ h₂ σ := le_trans (h₁ σ) (h₂ σ)
  le_antisymm F G h₁ h₂ := ext_weight (funext fun σ => le_antisymm (h₁ σ) (h₂ σ))

@[simp] theorem weight_le_iff (F G : Filtration α) :
    F ≤ G ↔ ∀ σ, F.weight σ ≤ G.weight σ := Iff.rfl

/-! ## The lattice structure -/

/-- The pointwise maximum of two filtrations: `max` preserves monotonicity and
`∅`-grounding, so it is again a filtration (Bridge IX's `ofWeight`). -/
def supFiltration (F G : Filtration α) : Filtration α :=
  ofWeight (fun σ => F.weight σ ⊔ G.weight σ)
    (sup_le F.weight_empty G.weight_empty)
    ((weight_monotone F).sup (weight_monotone G))

/-- The pointwise minimum of two filtrations. -/
def infFiltration (F G : Filtration α) : Filtration α :=
  ofWeight (fun σ => F.weight σ ⊓ G.weight σ)
    (le_trans inf_le_left F.weight_empty)
    ((weight_monotone F).inf (weight_monotone G))

-- !-- Reuse the `PartialOrder` instance; `sup := supFiltration`, `inf := infFiltration`.
-- !-- All six lattice axioms are pointwise `le_sup_left`/`sup_le`/`inf_le_left`/`le_inf`
-- !-- on the weights (the weights of `supFiltration`/`infFiltration` are `⊔`/`⊓` by
-- !-- `rfl`). -- !--
/-- **`Filtration α` is a lattice.**  Pointwise `max` and `min` of monotone,
`∅`-grounded weight functions are again monotone and `∅`-grounded (Bridge IX), so
the representation set is closed under `⊔`/`⊓` and `Filtration α` inherits the
pointwise lattice order. -/
instance instLatticeFiltration : Lattice (Filtration α) :=
  { instPartialOrderFiltration with
    sup := supFiltration
    inf := infFiltration
    le_sup_left := fun _ _ _ => le_sup_left
    le_sup_right := fun _ _ _ => le_sup_right
    sup_le := fun _ _ _ h₁ h₂ σ => sup_le (h₁ σ) (h₂ σ)
    inf_le_left := fun _ _ _ => inf_le_left
    inf_le_right := fun _ _ _ => inf_le_right
    le_inf := fun _ _ _ h₁ h₂ σ => le_inf (h₁ σ) (h₂ σ) }

@[simp] theorem weight_sup (F G : Filtration α) (σ : Finset α) :
    (F ⊔ G).weight σ = F.weight σ ⊔ G.weight σ := rfl

@[simp] theorem weight_inf (F G : Filtration α) (σ : Finset α) :
    (F ⊓ G).weight σ = F.weight σ ⊓ G.weight σ := rfl

/-! ## Order-functoriality of the pullback -/

/-
!-- Unfold `≤` and `pullback_weight`; `h (σ.image f)` is exactly the goal. -- !--

**Pullback is monotone (order-preserving).**  The contravariant persistence
functor of Bridge IX respects the pointwise order.
-/
theorem pullback_mono [DecidableEq β] (f : α → β) {F G : Filtration β} (h : F ≤ G) :
    pullback f F ≤ pullback f G := by
      exact fun σ => h _

/-
!-- `ext_weight`; both sides have weight `F.weight (σ.image f) ⊔ G.weight (σ.image f)`
!-- by `pullback_weight`/`weight_sup`. -- !--

**Pullback preserves joins.**  Precomposition with `·.image f` is pointwise, so
`pullback f` is a `⊔`-homomorphism.
-/
theorem pullback_sup [DecidableEq β] (f : α → β) (F G : Filtration β) :
    pullback f (F ⊔ G) = pullback f F ⊔ pullback f G := by
      convert ext_weight _;
      ext σ; simp +decide [ pullback_weight, weight_sup ] ;

/-
!-- `ext_weight`; both sides have weight `F.weight (σ.image f) ⊓ G.weight (σ.image f)`. -- !--

**Pullback preserves meets.**  `pullback f` is a `⊓`-homomorphism; together with
`pullback_sup` it is a lattice homomorphism.
-/
theorem pullback_inf [DecidableEq β] (f : α → β) (F G : Filtration β) :
    pullback f (F ⊓ G) = pullback f F ⊓ pullback f G := by
      exact ext_weight (by ext σ; simp [pullback_weight, weight_inf])

/-! ## The representation order isomorphism -/

/-
!-- `toEquiv := weightEquiv`; `map_rel_iff'` unfolds both sides to
!-- `∀ σ, F.weight σ ≤ G.weight σ` (`Subtype.coe_le_coe`, `Pi.le_def`), i.e. `Iff.rfl`. -- !--

**The representation is an order isomorphism.**  Bridge IX's bijection
`weightEquiv` upgrades to an iso of partial orders between `Filtration α` and the
monotone, `∅`-grounded functions under the pointwise order.
-/
def weightOrderIso : Filtration α ≃o {w : Finset α → ℝ // w ∅ ≤ 0 ∧ Monotone w} where
  toEquiv := weightEquiv
  map_rel_iff' := by
    simp +decide [ weightEquiv, Pi.le_def, weight_le_iff ]

/-! ## The metric–order bridge -/

/-
!-- By Bridge VIII `eInterleavingDist_eq_weightSupEDist` and `weightSupEDist`; for
!-- each `σ`, `h σ : F.weight σ ≤ G.weight σ` gives
!-- `|F.weight σ - G.weight σ| = G.weight σ - F.weight σ` (`abs_of_nonpos`/`abs_sub_comm`). -- !--

**The metric–order bridge.**  Between comparable filtrations the interleaving
distance is the supremum of the (nonnegative) weight *gap* — the absolute value of
Bridge VIII's isometry formula disappears.
-/
theorem eInterleavingDist_of_le (F G : Filtration α) (h : F ≤ G) :
    eInterleavingDist F G = ⨆ σ, ENNReal.ofReal (G.weight σ - F.weight σ) := by
      convert eInterleavingDist_eq_weightSupEDist F G using 1;
      convert ( iSup_congr fun σ => ?_ );
      rw [ abs_sub_comm, abs_of_nonneg ( sub_nonneg_of_le ( h σ ) ) ]

/-
!-- `eInterleavingDist_eq_weightSupEDist` on both sides; for each `σ`,
!-- `|F.weight σ - (F ⊔ G).weight σ| ≤ |F.weight σ - G.weight σ|` because
!-- `(F ⊔ G).weight σ = max (F.weight σ) (G.weight σ)` lies between them; conclude with
!-- `iSup`-monotonicity. -- !--

**The join is nonexpansive.**  Moving from `F` to `F ⊔ G` never increases the
distance from `F` beyond `eInterleavingDist F G`.
-/
theorem eInterleavingDist_sup_le (F G : Filtration α) :
    eInterleavingDist F (F ⊔ G) ≤ eInterleavingDist F G := by
      rw [ eInterleavingDist_eq_weightSupEDist, eInterleavingDist_eq_weightSupEDist ];
      refine' iSup_le fun σ => _;
      refine' le_trans _ ( le_iSup _ σ );
      cases le_total ( F.weight σ ) ( G.weight σ ) <;> simp +decide [ *, abs_of_nonneg, abs_of_nonpos ]

/-
!-- Symmetric to `eInterleavingDist_sup_le`, with `min` in place of `max`. -- !--

**The meet is nonexpansive.**  Moving from `F` to `F ⊓ G` never increases the
distance from `F` beyond `eInterleavingDist F G`.
-/
theorem eInterleavingDist_inf_le (F G : Filtration α) :
    eInterleavingDist F (F ⊓ G) ≤ eInterleavingDist F G := by
      rw [ eInterleavingDist_eq_weightSupEDist, eInterleavingDist_eq_weightSupEDist ];
      refine' iSup_mono fun σ => _;
      cases le_total ( F.weight σ ) ( G.weight σ ) <;> simp +decide [ *, weight_inf ]

/-! ## Faithfulness (Direction 5) -/

/-
!-- If `pullback f F = pullback f G` then `∀ σ, F.weight (σ.image f) = G.weight (σ.image f)`
!-- (`congrArg weight` + `pullback_weight`).  Surjectivity of `f` makes `σ ↦ σ.image f`
!-- surjective (use `Function.surjInv` as in `…_of_surjective`), so weights agree on
!-- every `τ`; conclude `F = G` by `ext_weight`. -- !--

**Pullback along a surjection is injective (faithfulness, Direction 5).**
Companion to Bridge IX's isometry-under-surjection: distinct filtrations have
distinct pullbacks along a surjection, so the persistence functor is faithful on the
subcategory of surjections.
-/
theorem pullback_injective_of_surjective [DecidableEq α] [DecidableEq β]
    (f : α → β) (hf : Function.Surjective f) :
    Function.Injective (pullback f : Filtration β → Filtration α) := by
      intro F G hFG
      have h_eq : ∀ σ : Finset α, F.weight (σ.image f) = G.weight (σ.image f) := by
        exact fun σ => by simpa using congr_arg ( fun F => F.weight σ ) hFG;
      refine' ext_weight ( funext fun τ => _ );
      convert h_eq ( Finset.image ( Function.surjInv hf ) τ ) using 1;
      · congr! 1;
        ext x; simp +decide [ Function.surjInv_eq hf ] ;
      · congr! 1;
        ext x; simp +decide [ Function.surjInv_eq hf ] ;

end Filtration

